<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>Stocks-Markets-Economic Times</title><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks</link><description><![CDATA[Stock Market News: Latest Stock news and updates on The Economic Times. Find Stock Market Live Updates, BSE, NSE Top Gainers, Losers and more.]]> </description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:29:30 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/2146842.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) 2026 Bennett Coleman and Co. Ltd, http://info.indiatimes.com/terms/tou.html</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>Economic Times</title><url>https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-76939477,width-600,height-60/economictimes.jpg</url><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Carlyle pares 7.4% stake in Piramal Pharma for over Rs 2,211 crore]]> </title><description><![CDATA[The Carlyle Group has divested 7.4 percent of its stake in Piramal Pharma through an open market deal, selling approximately 9.86 crore shares at an average rate of Rs 224.17 each. As a result, its stake decreased from 17.93 percent to 10.52 percent. Aditya Birla Sun Life Mutual Fund was the most significant buyer, acquiring over 2.12 crore shares. Subsequently, Piramal Pharma's share price dropped by 1.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/carlyle-pares-7-4-stake-in-piramal-pharma-for-over-rs-2211-crore/articleshow/136165837.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136165837,imgsize-19392.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/carlyle-pares-7-4-stake-in-piramal-pharma-for-over-rs-2211-crore/articleshow/136165837.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:32:44 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[SEBI eases KYC norms, centralises supplementary client data to simplify onboarding]]> </title><description><![CDATA[SEBI has revealed new measures aimed at simplifying the client onboarding process for investors. By centralising supplementary KYC details with KYC Registration Agencies, investors can avoid repetition. The revised framework will take effect on December 24, 2026, enhancing efficiency in data management. Intermediaries are instructed to report account closures promptly to maintain accurate KYC records. Investors are also advised against engaging with grey market premium figures for IPOs.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-eases-kyc-norms-centralises-supplementary-client-data-to-simplify-onboarding/articleshow/136162936.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136162936,imgsize-97308.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-eases-kyc-norms-centralises-supplementary-client-data-to-simplify-onboarding/articleshow/136162936.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:41:00 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sebi mulls early payout of up to 80% of sale proceeds to FPOs in commodity derivatives market]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Sebi introduced a proposal for an early pay-out framework designed to assist Farmer Producer Organisations. This framework would allow FPOs to access up to 80 percent of sale proceeds before contract expiry. The initiative aims to alleviate liquidity challenges by providing timely payments to farmers. Corporate trading members will offer this facility based on certain conditions and net worth requirements. Public comments on the proposal are invited until December 16.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-mulls-early-payout-of-up-to-80-of-sale-proceeds-to-fpos-in-commodity-derivatives-market/articleshow/136162861.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136162861,imgsize-168964.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-mulls-early-payout-of-up-to-80-of-sale-proceeds-to-fpos-in-commodity-derivatives-market/articleshow/136162861.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:39:04 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[RBI may opt for 25 bps rate hike as oil eases, inflation risks persist: Baroda BNP Paribas MF CIO]]> </title><description><![CDATA[The Reserve Bank of India is projected to implement a 0.25 percent interest rate hike in December. While decreasing crude oil prices could alleviate some inflation worries, many senior executives advocate for a measured strategy due to the prevailing economic climate. Nevertheless, concerns regarding food inflation and supply chain issues persist, adversely influencing overall forecasts.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/rbi-may-opt-for-25-bps-rate-hike-as-oil-eases-inflation-risks-persist-baroda-bnp-paribas-mf-cio/articleshow/136162711.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136162711,imgsize-113464.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/rbi-may-opt-for-25-bps-rate-hike-as-oil-eases-inflation-risks-persist-baroda-bnp-paribas-mf-cio/articleshow/136162711.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:36:00 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Shapoor Mistry lobbied Modi twice for Tata Sons IPO as battle over listing intensifies]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Shapoor Mistry, the head of the Shapoorji Pallonji Group, has reached out to Prime Minister Modi regarding the listing troubles faced by Tata Sons. He claims that Tata Trusts are obstructing the public offering for their own benefit and breaching regulations. Meanwhile, the Reserve Bank of India has pressured Tata Sons to meet listing necessities.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/mar